          "explanation": "(a) True: negative sampling replaces the full softmax over the vocabulary with a few sampled negatives. (b) False: Word2Vec has no vector for an out-of-vocabulary word either, so it is no better there. (c) False: that describes extrinsic evaluation; intrinsic evaluation tests the vectors directly (similarity, analogies). (d) False: rich morphology makes simple (whitespace) tokenization produce huge, sparse vocabularies.",
