          "modelAnswer": "Adapters let you adapt a large pretrained model to a new task cheaply. Small trainable modules (a bottleneck: project down to a small hidden size, nonlinearity, project back up, with a residual connection) are inserted into each layer. The pretrained weights are frozen and only the adapters are trained. So each new task needs only a few new parameters (stored separately per task), with less risk of catastrophic forgetting, instead of fine-tuning and storing the whole model.",
